1. To check the version – git –version
2. To check the hidden files(.file,.git…..) – ls -Force
3. To add the git into for directory or project – git init
4. To check the status of the files(if any changes made or modified files) – git status
5. The status are:
Untracked → new files not added to Git
Modified → tracked files changed but not staged.
Staged → the files added to the staging area, ready to commit.
Committed/Clean → no changes, everything saved
Staging area → a place where you put the changes you want to save. (git add)
Commit → the actual save of those changes into Git history. (git commit) 
Think of it like this:
● Staging area = packing items into a box.
● Commit = sealing the box and putting it on the shelf with a label.
